      'A preference for executing standard processes over abstract, unstructured problem-solving',
    ],
    whatYoudNeed: 'An MBA or PGDM in Strategy is often a material differentiator, and can be close to a hard prerequisite for direct entry into top strategy roles; Certified Management Consultant (CMC) is useful if aiming for consulting specifically. A CV must demonstrate the ability to analyse complex data, solve unstructured problems, and operate effectively with senior leadership.',
  ),
  CareerHandbookEntry(
    verticalName: 'Business Development & Strategic Sales',
    whatItDoes: 'This is the revenue engine — long-cycle, high-value, complex business-to-business sales and partnership-building rather than transactional selling. It exists to win major contracts, forge strategic partnerships and open new markets, directly driving the company\'s top-line growth.',
    careerRoadmap: 'The typical path starts with managing the relationship for one or more major clients, understanding their needs and renewing contracts. It grows to actively hunting new business — responding to major proposals, orchestrating pitch teams and negotiating complex pricing — before directing sales strategy for a vertical or region with a team of specialists reporting in. Senior tiers look beyond individual sales to strategic partnerships and new market entry, culminating in ownership of all revenue-generating functions across the enterprise.',
    whoSucceeds: [
      'Charismatic, resilient and highly persistent networkers',
