      'Experience in defence procurement or high-level liaison work translates well',
      'Ability to build rapid rapport with strangers',
    ],
    whoStruggles: [
      'Viewing \'sales\' as a dirty word',
      'Discomfort with compensation tied to performance outcomes',
      'Difficulty building rapport quickly with unfamiliar stakeholders',
    ],
    whatYoudNeed: 'Any graduate degree works, though an MBA is often preferred. Certified Sales Professional and Strategic Account Management (SAMA) certifications help bridge the gap. A CV should prove the ability to influence outcomes, manage complex multi-stakeholder relationships, and drive initiatives with quantifiable value.',
  ),
  CareerHandbookEntry(
    verticalName: 'HR, Talent Management & L&D',
    whatItDoes: 'Human Resources today is a strategic function focused on organisational capability, not just payroll and leave — it acquires, trains, evaluates and retains the people a business needs to run. Learning & Development builds the skills the workforce will need next, while talent management identifies and grooms future leaders.',
    careerRoadmap: 'Officers typically start as the HR partner to a specific business leader, handling grievances, appraisals, hiring and coaching managers. The role grows to managing more complex talent interventions, designing training curricula and handling workforce restructuring and succession planning, before owning HR or talent strategy for a major division and aligning it with business goals. At the senior tiers, the role shapes enterprise-wide culture and organisational design, culminating in advising the CEO on the organisation\'s overall people agenda.',
    whoSucceeds: [
