    ],
    whoStruggles: [
      'A preference for issuing orders over coaching',
      'Difficulty handling emotional workplace conflict',
      'Impatience with corporate compliance and grievance processes',
    ],
    whatYoudNeed: 'An HR-focused MBA is often preferred though not always mandatory. SHRM-CP and CIPD are globally recognised certifications that demonstrate familiarity with commercial HR frameworks and labour law. A CV should translate military leadership into HR terms — the scale of personnel managed, training architectures built, and experience with disciplinary or welfare systems.',
  ),
  CareerHandbookEntry(
    verticalName: 'Corporate Affairs, ESG & Public Policy',
    whatItDoes: 'This vertical manages a company\'s relationship with the outside world — governments, regulators, media and communities — and its environmental, social and governance commitments. It exists because external relationships and regulatory posture can materially affect a company\'s licence to operate, reputation and growth; it functions essentially as corporate diplomacy.',
    careerRoadmap: 'The typical path starts with handling ground-level relationships — local CSR projects, monitoring legislative change, drafting regional press materials. It grows to managing strategic stakeholder maps, policy submissions and PR crisis response, then to advocating at state or national level and building alliances with industry bodies. At the senior tiers, the role protects the enterprise\'s global licence to operate and, ultimately, becomes the public face of the company on regulatory and reputational matters alongside the CEO.',
    whoSucceeds: [
