    careerRoadmap: 'Officers typically start by supporting government liaison, tender documentation and stakeholder coordination. The role grows to managing important government relationships, bids and offset-related workstreams, then to owning major PSU or defence-business accounts and shaping procurement requirements in dialogue with military planning bodies. At the senior tiers, the officer leads business strategy across government-facing portfolios and, ultimately, provides board-level or advisory oversight on defence and government-business strategy.',
