  ),
  CareerHandbookEntry(
    verticalName: 'Corporate Governance',
    whatItDoes: 'Corporate governance makes sure a company is directed and controlled through clear rules, accountable decisions and accurate records, managing the mechanics of board meetings and statutory compliance. It exists because poor governance can lead to fraud, regulatory action, and loss of investor or stakeholder trust.',
    careerRoadmap: 'The typical path starts with handling the mechanics of compliance — drafting minutes, filing statutory returns, tracking compliance dashboards. It grows to managing the board\'s agenda and ensuring resolutions are legally sound, then to acting as primary advisor to the board on its legal duties and navigating governance requirements during major transactions. At the senior tiers, governance is integrated with broader enterprise risk, culminating in advising the chairman and CEO on the organisation\'s overall governance and accountability posture.',
    whoSucceeds: [
