  ),
  CareerHandbookEntry(
    verticalName: 'Tech Product & Data Operations',
    whatItDoes: 'This vertical builds and refines the digital tools a company uses or sells. Product management decides what software to build based on customer needs, while data operations ensures the data a business generates is clean, accessible and analysed to drive decisions. It exists to create competitive advantage through better digital products and data-driven insight.',
    careerRoadmap: 'Officers typically start as the bridge between business teams and engineers — writing requirements, managing delivery cycles and ensuring code ships on time. The role grows to owning a specific feature set or data pipeline, prioritising the engineering backlog, before scaling to owning the roadmap for a major product suite and leading teams of data scientists and product managers. At the senior tiers, the role aligns product vision with corporate strategy, culminating in ownership of the enterprise\'s overall digital product strategy.',
    whoSucceeds: [
